For each slot generation, stream ordering and the ready-event wait establish `producer → consumer`. Before reuse, the consumed-event wait establishes `previous consumer → next producer`. Each wait is submitted before its referenced event is re-recorded, so it captures the intended generation; no implicit stream dependency, device-wide synchronization, or host synchronization between iterations is needed.

